  Two deliberate choices worth flagging:

  - [1m[38;5;153merrors[39m is a per-field map, replacing today's single [38;5;153merror[39m string.[0m That's a breaking change to the one existing
    caller, which I'll migrate. Per-field is the point — a single string can't tell a form which input to mark.
  - [1m[38;5;153merrors[39m is always present[0m, [38;5;153m{}[39m when valid, so callers never branch on undefined.

  No DOM access anywhere in this file — that's the "compute only" boundary you picked. It's importable by a test runner
  as-is.

  Data flow is unchanged in shape: submit handler reads input values → builds a [38;5;153mvalues[39m object → calls [38;5;153mvalidate[39m →
  branches on [38;5;153m.valid[39m.

